---
title: File check
tags: tools
heading: "Check file type"
summary: >-
    Finds out what type up to 5 files really are, from the bytes each one starts with.
noLimits: true
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import fileFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>A file's name can say one thing and its header another, as when a file is renamed to hide it, and the check says when they disagree.</p>
    <p>Only the first 36 bytes of each file are read, in your browser, and nothing is uploaded or stored. Headers are matched against the <a href="/files/headers/" class="text-convrtr">File headers</a> list, which won't catch everything. Feel free to reach out if there's a header missing, or one you think would be worth adding.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call fileFrame(filename, "File check", formats = "any type, up to 5 at once", privacy = "Only the first 36 bytes of each file are read, in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.", multiple = true) %}{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
